## Joint distribution of the test statistics {.t}

\vspace{-0.82em}

\parskip=\dimexpr\parskip\relax plus \gluestretch\parskip

Ventricular shortening velocity (VSV, %/s) and fasting blood glucose (FBG, mmol/l) were measured in 24 type 1 diabetic patients (23 with complete data). The following two null hypotheses are tested:

$H_1$: $\mu_{\mathrm{VSV}} = 0$ at $\mathrm{FBG} = 0$

$H_2$: no linear association between FBG and VSV (i.e. $\mathrm{slope} = 0$)

\vspace{-0.5em}

\scriptsize\topsep=\dimexpr\topsep\relax plus \gluestretch\topsep\partopsep=\dimexpr\partopsep\relax plus \gluestretch\partopsep

```{r thuesen-lm-joint, echo=FALSE, message=FALSE}
library(ISwR)
data(thuesen)
thuesen <- thuesen[complete.cases(thuesen), ]
cf <- summary(lm(short.velocity ~ blood.glucose, data = thuesen))$coefficients
noquote(cbind(formatC(cf[, 1:3], format = "f", digits = 3), "Pr(>|t|)" = format.pval(cf[, 4], eps = 0.001, digits = 2)))
```

\vspace{-1.2em}

\\textcolor{gray}{Data: \texttt{thuesen} dataset (\texttt{ISwR} package v`r packageDescription("ISwR")$Version`, R `r paste(R.version$major, R.version$minor, sep = ".")`)}

\begin{tikzpicture}[remember picture, overlay]
\draw[-{Latex[length=6pt,width=4.5pt]}, thick, crukdark] ([xshift=240pt,yshift=-138.8pt]current page.north west) -- ([xshift=282pt,yshift=-138.8pt]current page.north west);
\draw[-{Latex[length=6pt,width=4.5pt]}, thick, crukdark] ([xshift=240pt,yshift=-147.8pt]current page.north west) -- ([xshift=282pt,yshift=-147.8pt]current page.north west);
\node[anchor=west, inner sep=0, text width=70pt, align=left, font=\scriptsize\bfseries, text=crukdark] at ([xshift=288pt,yshift=-143.3pt]current page.north west) {Under $\mathbfit{H}_{\mathbf{0}}^{\mathbf{global}}$,\\ we know the joint\\ distribution of the\\ test statistics};
\draw[-{Latex[length=6pt,width=4.5pt]}, thick, crukdark] ([xshift=323pt,yshift=-164.8pt]current page.north west) |- ([xshift=246pt,yshift=-196pt]current page.north west);
\end{tikzpicture}

\normalsize

\vspace{-3.25em}

```{r joint-t-contour, fig.width=3.3, fig.height=2.4, fig.align="center", out.width="34%"}
crukdark <- "#00007E"; cruklight <- "#009CEE"

## The two t statistics of the linear model are jointly bivariate-t:
## same residual df as the model, correlation taken from vcov(fit).
fit  <- lm(short.velocity ~ blood.glucose, data = thuesen)
nu   <- df.residual(fit)                       # 21
V    <- vcov(fit)
rho  <- V[1, 2] / sqrt(V[1, 1] * V[2, 2])      # -0.923

dbivt <- function(x, y, nu, rho) {
  q <- (x^2 - 2 * rho * x * y + y^2) / (1 - rho^2)
  (1 + q / nu)^(-(nu + 2) / 2) / (2 * pi * sqrt(1 - rho^2))
}

g  <- seq(-4, 4, length.out = 220)
z  <- outer(g, g, dbivt, nu = nu, rho = rho)
lv <- quantile(z[z > 0], probs = c(0.55, 0.75, 0.88, 0.95, 0.985))

par(mar = c(2.6, 2.8, 0.5, 0.5), mgp = c(1.5, 0.45, 0))
contour(g, g, z, levels = lv, drawlabels = FALSE,
        col = crukdark, lwd = 1.6, axes = FALSE,
        xlab = "", ylab = "", asp = 1)
axis(1, at = seq(-4, 4, 2), cex.axis = 0.85, lwd = 1.1)
axis(2, at = seq(-4, 4, 2), cex.axis = 0.85, lwd = 1.1, las = 1)
mtext(expression(italic(t)[1] ~ "(intercept)"), side = 1, line = 1.5, cex = 0.85)
mtext(expression(italic(t)[2] ~ "(blood glucose)"), side = 2, line = 1.7, cex = 0.85)
box(bty = "l", lwd = 1.1)
```

\begin{tikzpicture}[remember picture, overlay]
\node[anchor=south, inner sep=0, font=\footnotesize\bfseries] at ([yshift=10pt]current page.south) {Bivariate Student's $t$ distribution under $\mathbfit{H}_{\mathbf{0}}^{\mathbf{global}}$ ($\nu = `r nu`$, $\rho = `r sprintf("%.2f", rho)`$)};
\end{tikzpicture}

## The max-$t$ statistical principle {.t}

\vspace{-1pt}

$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Let $\mathcal{F} = \{H_1, H_2, \dots, H_n\}$ be a finite family of null hypotheses

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Let $\mathcal{D}$ be the joint distribution of the individual test statistics $t_1, t_2, \dots, t_n$ under $H_0^{\mathrm{global}}$ (i.e. all hypotheses are \colorbox{red}{\color{black}TRUE}). As in our example, the tests are two-sided: larger values of $|t_i|$ favour the rejection of $H_i$

\setlength{\abovedisplayskip}{2pt}\setlength{\belowdisplayskip}{2pt}$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Consider the maximum of the individual test statistics $t_i$: $$T_{\max} = \max_{i=1, 2, \dots, n} |t_i| \qquad (\text{one-sided tests: } T_{\max} = \max\nolimits_{i} t_i)$$

\vspace{-\parskip}
\begingroup\leftskip=9pt

The joint distribution $\mathcal{D}$ determines the distribution of $T_{\max}$ under $H_0^{\mathrm{global}}$:

\par
\endgroup

\vspace{-2.72em}

```{r maxt-distribution, fig.width=6.4, fig.height=1.92, fig.align="center", out.width="100%"}
crukdark <- "#00007E"; crukpink <- "#FF0087"

## T_max = max(|t_1|, |t_2|) for the two statistics of the PREVIOUS slide:
## a bivariate t with nu = 21 df and correlation rho = -0.92. The objects
## fit, nu and rho are carried over from the joint-t-contour chunk.
tobs <- summary(fit)$coefficients[, 3]
nmax <- length(tobs)
r2   <- sqrt(1 - rho^2)

## G(a) = P(|Z_1| <= a, |Z_2| <= a) on a grid, then F_max(x) = E_S[G(xS)]
## with S = sqrt(chi^2_nu / nu) independent of (Z_1, Z_2).
ag <- seq(0, 16, length.out = 700)
zg <- seq(-9, 9, length.out = 801); dz <- diff(zg)[1]
Gg <- vapply(ag, function(a) {
  z <- zg[abs(zg) <= a]
  if (!length(z)) return(0)
  sum(dnorm(z) * (pnorm((a - rho * z) / r2) -
                  pnorm((-a - rho * z) / r2))) * dz
}, numeric(1))

sg <- seq(0.25, 2.8, length.out = 500)
ws <- 2 * nu * sg * dchisq(nu * sg^2, df = nu) * diff(sg)[1]
Fmax <- function(x) sum(ws * approx(ag, Gg, xout = x * sg, rule = 2)$y)

qcrit <- uniroot(function(x) Fmax(x) - 0.95, c(0.5, 6))$root
xlim  <- c(0, 5.2)
xs    <- seq(xlim[1], xlim[2], length.out = 420)
Fsp   <- splinefun(xs, vapply(xs, Fmax, numeric(1)))
fmax  <- function(x) Fsp(x, deriv = 1)
ys    <- fmax(xs)

par(mar = c(3.1, 0.5, 0.9, 0.5), mgp = c(1.5, 0.45, 0))
plot(NULL, xlim = xlim, ylim = c(0, max(ys) * 2.10),
     axes = FALSE, xlab = "", ylab = "")

## the 5% rejection region in the upper tail
xr <- seq(qcrit, xlim[2], length.out = 300)
polygon(c(xr, rev(xr)), c(fmax(xr), rep(0, length(xr))),
        col = crukpink, border = NA)

lines(xs, ys, col = crukdark, lwd = 2)

axis(1, at = 0:5, cex.axis = 1.02, lwd = 1.1)
mtext(expression(T[max]), side = 1, line = 2.0, cex = 1.2)

yq <- fmax(qcrit)
segments(qcrit, 0, qcrit, yq, col = crukpink, lwd = 1.4)
text(qcrit - 0.26, fmax(qcrit - 0.26) + max(ys) * 0.42,
     bquote(q[alpha] == .(sprintf("%.2f", qcrit))),
     col = crukpink, cex = 1.0, adj = c(0.5, 0.5))
text(qcrit + 0.72, yq + max(ys) * 0.42, "5%", col = crukpink,
     cex = 0.92, adj = c(0.5, 0.5))

## pink "Critical region" box, sized to its text
lab <- "Critical region"; lcex <- 0.92
bx <- 3.9; by <- max(ys) * 0.62
bw <- strwidth(lab, cex = lcex) * 1.22
bh <- strheight(lab, cex = lcex) * 1.5
rect(bx - bw/2, by - bh, bx + bw/2, by + bh,
     border = crukpink, lwd = 1.4, col = "white")
text(bx, by, lab, col = crukpink, cex = lcex, font = 2)
arrows(bx - bw/2 * 0.35, by - bh, qcrit + 0.35, 0.012, length = 0.05,
       lwd = 1.2, col = crukpink)

text(2.1, max(ys) * 1.507,
     substitute("Distribution of" ~ T[max] ~ "(" * n == N * "," ~ nu == NU *
                "," ~ rho == RHO * ")",
                list(N = nmax, NU = nu, RHO = sprintf("%.2f", rho))),
     col = crukdark, cex = 1.03)
```

\vspace{-0.75em}

\begingroup\scriptsize\\textcolor{gray}{Data: \texttt{thuesen} dataset (\texttt{ISwR} package v`r packageDescription("ISwR")$Version`, R `r paste(R.version$major, R.version$minor, sep = ".")`)}

\par\endgroup

## The max-$t$ statistical principle {.t}

\vspace{-1pt}

$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Consider the positions of the statistics $|t_1|, |t_2|, \dots, |t_n|$:

\vspace{\dimexpr-0.4em-9pt\relax}

```{r maxt-line, fig.width=6.4, fig.height=1.92, fig.align="center", out.width="100%"}
## EXACTLY the plot of the previous slide (xlim, xs, ys, fmax, qcrit, nmax,
## nu, rho and tobs are carried over from the maxt-distribution chunk),
## with only the two observed statistics added
par(mar = c(3.1, 0.5, 0.9, 0.5), mgp = c(1.5, 0.45, 0))
plot(NULL, xlim = xlim, ylim = c(0, max(ys) * 2.10),
     axes = FALSE, xlab = "", ylab = "")

## the 5% rejection region in the upper tail
xr <- seq(qcrit, xlim[2], length.out = 300)
polygon(c(xr, rev(xr)), c(fmax(xr), rep(0, length(xr))),
        col = crukpink, border = NA)

lines(xs, ys, col = crukdark, lwd = 2)

axis(1, at = 0:5, cex.axis = 1.02, lwd = 1.1)
mtext(expression(T[max]), side = 1, line = 2.0, cex = 1.2)

yq <- fmax(qcrit)
segments(qcrit, 0, qcrit, yq, col = crukpink, lwd = 1.4)
text(qcrit - 0.26, fmax(qcrit - 0.26) + max(ys) * 0.42,
     bquote(q[alpha] == .(sprintf("%.2f", qcrit))),
     col = crukpink, cex = 1.0, adj = c(0.5, 0.5))
text(qcrit + 0.72, yq + max(ys) * 0.42, "5%", col = crukpink,
     cex = 0.92, adj = c(0.5, 0.5))

## pink "Critical region" box, sized to its text
lab <- "Critical region"; lcex <- 0.92
bx <- 3.9; by <- max(ys) * 0.62
bw <- strwidth(lab, cex = lcex) * 1.22
bh <- strheight(lab, cex = lcex) * 1.5
rect(bx - bw/2, by - bh, bx + bw/2, by + bh,
     border = crukpink, lwd = 1.4, col = "white")
text(bx, by, lab, col = crukpink, cex = lcex, font = 2)
arrows(bx - bw/2 * 0.35, by - bh, qcrit + 0.35, 0.012, length = 0.05,
       lwd = 1.2, col = crukpink)

## the two statistics of the previous slide, with their adjusted p-values
padj <- vapply(abs(tobs), function(x) 1 - Fmax(x), numeric(1))
vlab <- sprintf("%.2f", abs(tobs))
tcex <- 0.90
x0   <- 2.46
text(x0, max(ys) * 1.78,
     bquote("|" * italic(t)[2] * "|" == .(vlab[2]) * "," ~~
            tilde(italic(p))[2] == .(formatC(padj[2], format = "f", digits = 3))),
     col = crukdark, cex = tcex, adj = c(0, 0.5))
text(x0, max(ys) * 1.36,
     bquote("|" * italic(t)[1] * "|" == .(vlab[1]) * "," ~~
            tilde(italic(p))[1] < 0.001),
     col = crukdark, cex = tcex, adj = c(0, 0.5))

```

\vspace{-0.7em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ $H_1$ is \textbf{rejected}: $|t_1| = 9.34 > q_\alpha = 2.23$, adjusted $\tilde{p}_1 < 0.001$\newline $H_2$ is \textbf{not rejected}: $|t_2| = 2.10 < q_\alpha = 2.23$, adjusted $\tilde{p}_2 = 0.064 > 0.05$

\par

\vspace{\dimexpr0.1em+9pt\relax}

\small \textbf{Subset pivotality condition}: take \textbf{any} subset $K$ of the hypotheses. Their statistics $\{t_i : i \in K\}$ must behave the same way when only the hypotheses in $K$ are \colorbox{red}{\color{black}TRUE} as they do when \textbf{all} of them are \colorbox{red}{\color{black}TRUE}\normalsize

\vspace{\dimexpr-0.4em+5.5pt\relax}

\begingroup\centering\small\textbf{Under the subset pivotality condition, the FWER is controlled ($\mathrm{FWER} \leq \alpha$)}

\par\endgroup

## Dunnett's test {.t}

\vspace{-1pt}

$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Statistical model}: one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA)

\vspace{-1.2em}

```{r dunnett-anova, fig.width=6.8, fig.height=1.85, fig.align="center", out.width="92%"}
crukdark <- "#00007E"; cruklight <- "#009CEE"; crukpink <- "#FF0087"

sig <- 0.55
mus <- c(0, 2.6, 4.4, 7.4)
labs <- list(expression("Control " * mu[0]), expression("Arm 1 " * mu[1]),
             expression("Arm 2 " * mu[2]), expression("Arm " * italic(n) * " " * mu[italic(n)]))
cols <- c(crukpink, cruklight, cruklight, cruklight)

par(mar = c(1.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.3))
plot(NULL, xlim = c(-1.6, 14.6), ylim = c(0, dnorm(0, 0, sig) * 1.08),
     axes = FALSE, xlab = "", ylab = "")
segments(-1.6, 0, 9.2, 0, col = "grey40", lwd = 1)
for (k in seq_along(mus)) {
  xs <- seq(mus[k] - 3.2 * sig, mus[k] + 3.2 * sig, length.out = 300)
  polygon(c(xs, rev(xs)), c(dnorm(xs, mus[k], sig), rep(0, length(xs))),
          col = adjustcolor(cols[k], 0.18), border = NA)
  lines(xs, dnorm(xs, mus[k], sig), col = cols[k], lwd = 2)
  segments(mus[k], 0, mus[k], dnorm(mus[k], mus[k], sig), col = cols[k], lty = 2, lwd = 1)
  mtext(labs[[k]], side = 1, line = 0.25, at = mus[k], cex = 0.78, col = cols[k])
}
text(5.9, 0.12, expression(cdots), cex = 1.4, col = crukdark)

## the two assumptions, in boxes on the right
## equal-width boxes, stacked down from the top of the plot region
box_stack <- function(txts, cx = 0.95) {
  bw  <- max(sapply(txts, strwidth, cex = cx)) * 1.12
  bh  <- max(sapply(txts, strheight, cex = cx)) * 1.5
  gap <- bh * 0.18
  x   <- par("usr")[2] - bw/2          # right-aligned to the plot region
  ys  <- par("usr")[4] - bh/2 - (seq_along(txts) - 1) * (bh + gap)
  par(xpd = NA)
  for (i in seq_along(txts)) {
    rect(x - bw/2, ys[i] - bh/2, x + bw/2, ys[i] + bh/2,
         border = crukdark, lwd = 1.3, col = "white")
    text(x, ys[i], txts[[i]], cex = cx, col = crukdark, font = 2)
  }
}
box_stack(list(
  expression(bold("Normality: ") * Y[ki] %~% N(mu[k], sigma^2)),
  expression(bold("Equal variances: ") * "same " * sigma^2),
  expression(bold("Independence: ") * Y[ki] * " mutually independent")))
```

\vspace{-1.3em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Hypotheses}: }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Hypotheses}: $H_k : \mu_k = \mu_0$, $k = 1, \dots, n$\vspace{3.5pt}\newline {\fontsize{10.5pt}{12.5pt}\selectfont For each of the $n$ arms, the arm mean equals the control mean $\mu_0$

\par

}

\vspace{0.25em}

\vspace{0.25em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Each $t_k$ follows a Student's $t$ distribution with $N - (n+1)$ degrees of freedom under $H_k$\newline \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}$\mathcal{D}$} is a multivariate Student's $t$ distribution under $H_0^{\mathrm{global}}$

\vspace{-1pt}

\noindent\hspace\*{14.5pt}\\tikz[baseline=-0.55ex, overlay]{\\draw[-{Latex[length=5pt,width=4pt]}, thick, crukdark] (0,9.5pt) -- (0,0) -- (16pt,0);}\\hspace{20pt}\\textbf{\\textcolor{crukdark}{The max-\$t\$ principle is applied to \$\\mathcal{D}\$}}

\par

## Tukey's test {.t}

\vspace{-1pt}

$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Statistical model}: one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA)

\vspace{-1.2em}

```{r tukey-anova, fig.width=6.8, fig.height=1.72, fig.align="center", out.width="92%"}
crukdark <- "#00007E"; cruklight <- "#009CEE"; crukpink <- "#FF0087"

sig <- 0.55
mus <- c(0, 2.8, 5.3, 8.3)
labs <- list(expression("Group 1 " * mu[1]), expression("Group 2 " * mu[2]),
             expression("Group 3 " * mu[3]), expression("Group " * italic(k) * " " * mu[italic(k)]))
cols <- c(cruklight, cruklight, cruklight, cruklight)

par(mar = c(1.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.3))
plot(NULL, xlim = c(-1.6, 15.6), ylim = c(0, dnorm(0, 0, sig) * 1.08),
     axes = FALSE, xlab = "", ylab = "")
segments(-1.6, 0, 10.1, 0, col = "grey40", lwd = 1)
for (k in seq_along(mus)) {
  xs <- seq(mus[k] - 3.2 * sig, mus[k] + 3.2 * sig, length.out = 300)
  polygon(c(xs, rev(xs)), c(dnorm(xs, mus[k], sig), rep(0, length(xs))),
          col = adjustcolor(cols[k], 0.18), border = NA)
  lines(xs, dnorm(xs, mus[k], sig), col = cols[k], lwd = 2)
  segments(mus[k], 0, mus[k], dnorm(mus[k], mus[k], sig), col = cols[k], lty = 2, lwd = 1)
  mtext(labs[[k]], side = 1, line = 0.25, at = mus[k], cex = 0.78, col = cols[k])
}
text(6.8, 0.12, expression(cdots), cex = 1.4, col = crukdark)

## the two assumptions, in boxes on the right
## equal-width boxes, stacked down from the top of the plot region
box_stack <- function(txts, cx = 0.95) {
  bw  <- max(sapply(txts, strwidth, cex = cx)) * 1.12
  bh  <- max(sapply(txts, strheight, cex = cx)) * 1.5
  gap <- bh * 0.18
  x   <- par("usr")[2] - bw/2          # right-aligned to the plot region
  ys  <- par("usr")[4] - bh/2 - (seq_along(txts) - 1) * (bh + gap)
  par(xpd = NA)
  for (i in seq_along(txts)) {
    rect(x - bw/2, ys[i] - bh/2, x + bw/2, ys[i] + bh/2,
         border = crukdark, lwd = 1.3, col = "white")
    text(x, ys[i], txts[[i]], cex = cx, col = crukdark, font = 2)
  }
}
box_stack(list(
  expression(bold("Normality: ") * Y[ji] %~% N(mu[j], sigma^2)),
  expression(bold("Equal variances: ") * "same " * sigma^2),
  expression(bold("Independence: ") * Y[ji] * " mutually independent")))
```

\vspace{-1.3em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Hypotheses}: }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Hypotheses}: $H_{j\ell} : \mu_j = \mu_\ell$, $1 \leq j < \ell \leq k$\vspace{1.5pt}\newline {\fontsize{10.5pt}{12.5pt}\selectfont For each of the $n = k(k-1)/2$ pairs, the two group means are equal

\par

}

\vspace{0.25em}

\vspace{0.25em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Each $t_{j\ell}$ follows a Student's $t$ distribution with $N - k$ degrees of freedom under $H_{j\ell}$\newline \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}$\mathcal{D}$} is a multivariate Student's $t$ distribution under $H_0^{\mathrm{global}}$

\vspace{-1pt}

\noindent\hspace\*{14.5pt}\\tikz[baseline=-0.55ex, overlay]{\\draw[-{Latex[length=5pt,width=4pt]}, thick, crukdark] (0,9.5pt) -- (0,0) -- (16pt,0);}\\hspace{20pt}\\textbf{\\textcolor{crukdark}{The max-\$t\$ principle is applied to \$\\mathcal{D}\$}}

\par

## \fontsize{15.5}{18}\selectfont Dunnett's test with unequal variances (Hasler--Hothorn) {.t}

\vspace{-1pt}

$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Statistical model}: one-way ANOVA \textbf{without} the equal-variance assumption

\vspace{-1.2em}

```{r dunnett-unequalvar, fig.width=6.8, fig.height=1.85, fig.align="center", out.width="92%"}
crukdark <- "#00007E"; cruklight <- "#009CEE"; crukpink <- "#FF0087"

sigs <- c(0.40, 0.78, 0.50, 0.92)
mus  <- c(0, 2.6, 4.4, 7.4)
labs <- list(expression("Control " * mu[0]), expression("Arm 1 " * mu[1]),
             expression("Arm 2 " * mu[2]), expression("Arm " * italic(n) * " " * mu[italic(n)]))
cols <- c(crukpink, cruklight, cruklight, cruklight)

par(mar = c(1.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.3))
plot(NULL, xlim = c(-1.6, 14.6), ylim = c(0, dnorm(0, 0, min(sigs)) * 1.08),
     axes = FALSE, xlab = "", ylab = "")
segments(-1.6, 0, 9.2, 0, col = "grey40", lwd = 1)
for (k in seq_along(mus)) {
  xs <- seq(mus[k] - 3.2 * sigs[k], mus[k] + 3.2 * sigs[k], length.out = 300)
  polygon(c(xs, rev(xs)), c(dnorm(xs, mus[k], sigs[k]), rep(0, length(xs))),
          col = adjustcolor(cols[k], 0.18), border = NA)
  lines(xs, dnorm(xs, mus[k], sigs[k]), col = cols[k], lwd = 2)
  segments(mus[k], 0, mus[k], dnorm(mus[k], mus[k], sigs[k]), col = cols[k], lty = 2, lwd = 1)
  mtext(labs[[k]], side = 1, line = 0.25, at = mus[k], cex = 0.78, col = cols[k])
}
text(5.9, dnorm(0, 0, min(sigs)) * 0.25, expression(cdots), cex = 1.4, col = crukdark)

box_stack <- function(txts, cx = 0.95) {
  bw  <- max(sapply(txts, strwidth, cex = cx)) * 1.12
  bh  <- max(sapply(txts, strheight, cex = cx)) * 1.5
  gap <- bh * 0.18
  x   <- par("usr")[2] - bw/2
  ys  <- par("usr")[4] - bh/2 - (seq_along(txts) - 1) * (bh + gap)
  par(xpd = NA)
  for (i in seq_along(txts)) {
    rect(x - bw/2, ys[i] - bh/2, x + bw/2, ys[i] + bh/2,
         border = crukdark, lwd = 1.3, col = "white")
    text(x, ys[i], txts[[i]], cex = cx, col = crukdark, font = 2)
  }
}

box_stack(list(
  expression(bold("Normality: ") * Y[ki] %~% N(mu[k], sigma[k]^2)),
  expression(bold("Unequal variances: ") * sigma[k]^2 * " may differ"),
  expression(bold("Independence: ") * Y[ki] * " mutually independent")))
```

\vspace{-1.3em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Hypotheses}: }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}Hypotheses}: $H_k : \mu_k = \mu_0$, $k = 1, \dots, n$\vspace{3.5pt}\newline {\fontsize{10.5pt}{12.5pt}\selectfont For each of the $n$ arms, the arm mean equals the control mean $\mu_0$

\par

}

\vspace{0.25em}

\settowidth{\hangindent}{$\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ }\hangafter=1 $\textcolor{crukdark}{\bullet}$ Each $t_k$ (Welch) follows \textbf{approximately} a Student's $t$ distribution under $H_k$\newline \colorbox{cruklight}{\color{white}$\mathcal{D}$} is \textbf{approximately} a multivariate Student's $t$ distribution under $H_0^{\mathrm{global}}$

\vspace{-1pt}

\noindent\hspace\*{14.5pt}\\tikz[baseline=-0.55ex, overlay]{\\draw[-{Latex[length=5pt,width=4pt]}, thick, crukdark] (0,9.5pt) -- (0,0) -- (16pt,0);}\\hspace{20pt}\\textbf{\\textcolor{crukdark}{The max-\$t\$ principle is applied to \$\\mathcal{D}\$}}

\par

\vspace{\dimexpr0.3em+6.6pt\relax}

\begingroup\small\noindent\setlength{\fboxsep}{3.5pt}\fcolorbox{crukpink}{white}{\parbox{\dimexpr\linewidth-2\fboxsep-2\fboxrule\relax}{\centerline{\textbf{\textcolor{crukdark}{Tamhane's T2}} and \textbf{\textcolor{crukdark}{Dunnett's T3}} treat $\mathcal{D}$ \textbf{marginally} (each statistic on its own, not jointly)}}}

\par\endgroup

## \fontsize{15.5}{18}\selectfont Tukey's test with unequal variances (Hasler--Hothorn) {.t}

